// Vector 0 - ANCHOR. A BTC-style header; the original regression guard.
// Vector 1 - FMA SENTINEL. Same header with nNonce = 1, so it shares the anchor's
//   structure and matrix. Its digest changes if the compiler stops contracting
//   a*b+c into FMA -- which vector 0 cannot detect, being one of the ~28% of
//   headers that are contraction-insensitive. Consensus needs contraction ON, so
//   this vector fails the miner closed on -ffp-contract=off, a non-FMA target
//   (-march=x86-64, pre-Haswell), or GCC >= 14 (which honours the FP_CONTRACT
//   pragma that older GCC ignores). A non-contracting build yields, for diagnosis:
//     0c1029972b91faa9b05b7619098207b43c4dba41f7d1a4ebe605601b0f9086d8
//
// Both vectors are byte-identical across glibc 2.27 / 2.31 / 2.35 and GCC 7.5 /
// 11.4 on x86-64 (checked 2026-07-30), so neither is libm-version-fragile.
